# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Secrets / local env (keep examples) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# --- Transient files: scratch/ ---
# The bucket for anything that passes "could I delete this right now and lose
# nothing?" — session exports, tool output, generated diffs, debugging
# screenshots. Contents are never tracked; the README always is, so the
# membership test ships in a fresh clone and the directory is real rather than
# an empty claim. Rules: scratch/README.md
scratch/*
!scratch/README.md

# --- Scratch files, by name: the backstop ---
# Superseded as the primary mechanism by scratch/ above, and kept because the
# habit migrates and someone will always scratch in place. Name patterns can
# only enumerate, and the enumeration is the bug — the first file that motivated
# the directory was called `dev_setup.md`, which matches nothing below.
#
# Historically a credential-leak vector: a scratch file is where someone pastes a
# secret "just for a second" while wiring an OAuth app. Un-anchored deliberately —
# the habit migrates between directories, so these match at any depth. Note that
# ignoring a file protects the remote, never your disk or your backups.
tmp.md
tmp.*.md
**/tmp.md
**/tmp.html
2do.md
**/2do.md

# --- Node ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log

# --- Python ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- CDK ---
cdk.out/
.cdk.staging/
cdk-outputs.json

# --- Claude local overrides ---
.claude/settings.local.json
